<title>GERMANY: East German Jan ind orders fall 0.4 pct.</title>
<headline>East German Jan ind orders fall 0.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Jan 97     Dec 96     Jan 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   -0.4	 +0.5	-10.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +10.8	 -0.1	 -0.1</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		132.0	132.5	119.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				  Jan 97    Dec 96    Jan 97 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders	     -4.3	 +1.1     145.7</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Dec 96/Jan 97 with Nov/Oct 96:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  +2.5</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Dec 96/Jan 97 with Dec 95/Jan 96:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  +1.9</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 -2.0</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +20.9</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +6.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			   -2.9</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    -0.7</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
